{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_bc",
    "description": "Hybrid WENO5/ENO1 upwind first derivative d u/dx on cartesian_uniform_2d with the linear-extrapolation halo closure -- the per-axis derivative diff2x of NCAR fire_behavior's default level-set scheme (fire_upwinding = 9; Munoz-Esparza et al. 2018): fifth-order Jiang-Shu WENO5 in a band of weno_band_cells cells around the zero level set, first-order ENO1 (minmod) elsewhere and within bdy_eno1_cells of the walls, upwind side of the WENO reconstruction chosen by the wind-relative propagation sign signo = (grad4 u . (wind_u, wind_v)) d4 u/dx. This is the quantity fire_behavior feeds both to |grad psi| = sqrt(diff2x^2 + diff2y^2) and to the front normal nvx = diff2x/sqrt(|grad psi|^2 + eps); rules/weno5_eno1_norm_D2_extrapolate_bc packages the norm as a compound match so a consumer may write the norm as sqrt((D(u,x))^2 + (D(u,y))^2) and the normal's ingredients as bare D(u, wrt: x) / D(u, wrt: y) with the same scheme. Match D(u, wrt: x) at priority 10 (before the priority-less centered central_D1x_* rules if a document imports both), scoped with where {u: {shape: [x, y]}} (esm-spec 9.6.1). THE SCHEME: the body applies rules/weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame -- the seven-region makearray shared by this family, with its ENO1 strips and guarded-extrapolation wall lines -- around the imported stencils/weno5_eno1_D1x_interior on the doubly-interior block [4, NX-3] x [3, NY-2] (the hybrid switch on the field and the index, see that stencil). The frame's regions are lint-tiled (L006) in the frame's own file. BOUNDARY CLOSURE bc:extrapolate_linear: one-cell guarded linear-extrapolation ghosts at the x walls -- fire_behavior's Extrapol_var_at_bdys; see the frame. FREE NAMES (consumer-supplied, resolved in the consuming model's scope like the grid geometry dx, dy): wind_u, wind_v ([x, y] fields, the advecting wind), bdy_eno1_cells (>= 3; fire_behavior's BDY_ENO1 = 10), weno_band_cells (fire_behavior's fire_lsm_band_ngp = 4). Both ifelse branches are evaluated on every interior cell (esm ifelse is not lazy); the region structure keeps every evaluated index in range. Requires NX >= 7, NY >= 5 (respectively NY >= 7, NX >= 5 for the y rule). ORDER: formally first (ENO1 strips and far field); fifth in the smooth part of the WENO band away from critical points. EXACT on a linear field u = a x + b y + c on every cell except the wall toward which the field decreases along x (i = 1 for a > 0, i = NX for a < 0): there the guarded extrapolation clamps the ghost to the inner neighbour, so the two one-sided differences have opposite signs and the ENO1 minmod returns 0 instead of a -- fire_behavior's own wall behaviour, reproduced (the ghost is the plain linear one, and the result exact, only at a wall the field increases toward). Tagged order:1. The consumer's units checker sees a derivative of u per unit length.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:D",
      "axes:x,y",
      "order:1",
      "stencil_width:7",
      "bc:extrapolate_linear",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Munoz-Esparza, D., Kosovic, B., Jimenez, P. A., & Coen, J. L. (2018). An accurate fire-spread algorithm in the Weather Research and Forecasting model using the level-set method. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 10(4), 908-926. The hybrid WENO5/ENO1 level-set scheme (fire_upwinding = 9) of WRF-Fire / NCAR fire_behavior.",
        "doi": "10.1002/2017MS001108"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Shu, C.-W. (1996). Efficient implementation of weighted ENO schemes. Journal of Computational Physics, 126(1), 202-228. The classical WENO5 smoothness indicators beta_k and nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2.",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1996.0130"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Harten, A., Engquist, B., Osher, S., & Chakravarthy, S. R. (1987). Uniformly high order accurate essentially non-oscillatory schemes, III. Journal of Computational Physics, 71(2), 231-303. ENO stencil selection by smallest divided difference (first-order form: the minmod limiter).",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(87)90031-3"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls, Select_eno, Select_weno5, Select_4th, Select_godunov (case 4), Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame.esm"
    },
    {
      "ref": "../stencils/weno5_eno1_D1x_interior.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_bc": {
      "params": [
        "u"
      ],
      "priority": 10,
      "match": {
        "op": "D",
        "args": [
          "u"
        ],
        "wrt": "x"
      },
      "where": {
        "u": {
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ]
        }
      },
      "body": {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "weno5_eno1_D1x_extrapolate_frame",
        "bindings": {
          "u": "u",
          "interior": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "weno5_eno1_D1x_interior",
            "bindings": {
              "u": "u"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
